    {
      "id": "claim_3bb1c76ad86c45b7ad7a858240bc78b3",
      "statement": "The server uses MCP's Streamable HTTP transport in stateless mode: for every /mcp request, httpTransport.ts creates a fresh McpServer (via the factory passed from index.ts) and a fresh StreamableHTTPServerTransport with sessionIdGenerator: undefined, then connects and handles the request. This keeps the read-only server stateless because each tool call is a self-contained lookup against the shared immutable in-memory store; the expensive store/embedder are created once at startup and captured in the factory closure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/index.ts#L48-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:deb799cc379e096a49322148c5c693acfeb7f7252737f2cf0aa635dd1d2ab11c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/mcp/httpTransport.ts#L39-L68",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:df72e314f44190d547a9ea0c5df605e08d8d2042cd03f12b2a6144441521adfc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a37f6f236ffe4bbe9ca2a9ff08ae126b",
      "statement": "The HTTP surface is GET /health returning { status:'ok' } (no auth, used by the Docker HEALTHCHECK) and POST/GET/DELETE /mcp behind authMiddleware; responses are delivered as text/event-stream (SSE) with the JSON-RPC envelope in the data: line, which clients must parse.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://mcp-server/src/mcp/httpTransport.ts#L42-L68",
