    {
      "id": "claim_3ad8252aad7547fb8af8022a441e9874",
      "statement": "Content is baked into the Docker image as flat docs/pages, docs/partials, docs/examples folders pointed at by DOCS_ROOT/PARTIALS_ROOT/EXAMPLES_ROOT, and indexing happens at container startup; therefore serving updated docs requires rebuilding and redeploying the image (an accepted trade-off), and a cache hit lets a warm restart skip the embeddings API entirely.",
